      {
        i === 0 ? (
          <Notes time="0:45" cue="Ask the room to find the invented story before you press the arrow for the marks.">
            <p>
              The tool's output as returned, split by columns over two slides
              so every cell stays readable; nothing is abbreviated. The first
              arrow press marks it up.
            </p>
            <p>
              The main miss is the teaching point. The page says the project
              "involves enhancing Ephira's functionality", yet the walking
              skeleton and much of Release 1 re-plan what the app already did:
              the passcode and biometric lock, logging a day, the calendar,
              editing past entries, the filter, even a first prediction.
            </p>
            <p>
              Missed, out of scope: "Shareable doctor reports". The inherited
              export screen already offered a PDF, which it describes as
              "convenient for viewing and sharing", and opened the phone's
              share sheet. Invented: "Show fertile window" appears nowhere in
              the proposal. Misread: the proposal says "Start design and
              implementation of pregnancy tracking"; the tool cut it to a
              design doc and stated that as settled.
            </p>
          </Notes>
        ) : (
          <Notes time="0:45" cue="Point at the TestFlight card: the app had been in both stores since winter of the first team's year.">
            <p>
