              build into the stores' test tracks, for an app that was already
              in both stores when the advertised team took it over. Its
              reminders, backups, and
              store updates match the advertised work; they're the columns
              where the proposal and the repository agree.
            </p>
            <p>
              The lesson for the room: the tool's map looks finished, which is
              the danger. It had the proposal and nothing else, the same as a
              team that never opens the repository. Treat its output as a draft
              full of unflagged question marks, and check each one against
              the code and with the partner.
            </p>
